WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:07.319
Speaker 1: Democrats in the Senate, led, of
course, by Bernie Sanders and Elizabeth Warren,

00:00:07.319 --> 00:00:16.190
are pushing a draft for the reconciliation
package that would include five hundred billion

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:22.079
dollars that would be collected from fossil
fuel companies to pay for the emissions that

00:00:22.079 --> 00:00:26.429
they spewed out from the years 2000 to 2019.

00:00:26.429 --> 00:00:33.340
Now, Chuck Schumer, for the record, has stayed
mum on whether or not he is going to include

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:39.200
this five hundred billion dollar fine, essentially
on fossil fuel companies to pay for their

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.570
emissions.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:42.740
But why not write?

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:49.980
I mean, heck, one of the big issues we're
having with this reconciliation bill is it's

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.260
it's very expensive.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:52.680
How are we going to cover the cost?

00:00:52.680 --> 00:01:00.650
Well, if it's three and a half trillion, we
can pay for that half by putting this provision

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:02.350
in there.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:07.830
The fossil fuel companies, as has been widely
reported, have known about the dangers of

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:11.680
climate change since at least the 1970s.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:17.110
I've actually gone through the documents for
some reporting back when I was with the smog

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.110
blog.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:23.620
And actually they do have documents going
all the way back to the 1950s where they talk

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:29.540
about the fact that we believe that the burning
that we're doing of these fuels could possibly

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:32.140
be changing the actual atmosphere.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:33.140
It's remarkable.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.800
And I know everybody says that they've known
since the 1970s.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:39.870
But if you go through those documents, their
internal documents, they've actually been

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.909
concerned about this since the 50s.

00:01:41.909 --> 00:01:46.159
It was just really confirmed for them in the
70s.

00:01:46.159 --> 00:01:51.140
So either way, they have known about the dangers
of fossil fuel burning.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:52.930
They have known what it does to this planet.

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:59.750
And yes, it is time for them to pay us back,
because these are missions that go out there,

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:04.860
these extreme weather events that we see as
a result of climate change, they cost money.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.799
They cost lives.

00:02:06.799 --> 00:02:13.310
And yet, instead of making these industries
pay for it, we're subsidizing them to the

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:19.760
tune of, I think, direct cash subsidies at
14 billion a year at this point.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.630
This is nuts.

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:24.120
It's time for them to pay up.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:29.700
And this draft that is not yet in the reconciliation
bill, but they want to get it in the reconciliation

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:37.590
bill, but this draft would absolutely be a
great start to get us where we need to be

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.450
on this issue.

